  "title": "Big Line or Big Clique in Planar Point Sets",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $S$ be a set of points in the plane. Two points $v$ and $w$ in $S$ are visible with respect to $S$ if the line segment between $v$ and $w$ contains no other point in $S$.\n\nConjecture For all integers $k,\\ell\\geq2$ there is an integer $n$ such that every set of at least $n$ points in the plane contains at least $\\ell$ collinear points or $k$ pairwise visible points.",
